  "notes": "しゃがむ describes lowering oneself into a squatting position with both feet flat on the ground. This is a common posture in Japanese culture, often used when resting, working at ground level, or waiting.\n\nCONJUGATION (godan verb):\n- しゃがむ (dictionary form)\n- しゃがまない (negative)\n- しゃがんだ (past)\n- しゃがんで (te-form)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- しゃがみ⟦{込|こ}む→込む：00719_komu⟧: to squat down and stay (more prolonged action)",
